# Pong

One player against the computer, in the browser. First to 5 points wins.

## Start the game

Either:

- **Serve it** (recommended; needed for the web font): from this directory run
  `python3 -m http.server 8000` and open <http://localhost:8000/>; or
- **Open the file**: double-click `index.html` (works from `file://`, no install).

No build step and no dependencies: plain HTML5 canvas + JavaScript.

## Controls

| Key | Action |
|---|---|
| Enter / Space (or click) | Start from the title screen; play again from the result screen |
| W / S or ↑ / ↓ | Move your paddle (left) |
| P or Esc | Pause / resume |
| Esc on the result screen | Back to the title screen |
| M | Mute / unmute |

## Layout

- `index.html` — page and canvas (800 x 500 logical px, scaled to the window)
- `src/game.js` — rules: ball physics, computer opponent, scoring, first to 5
- `src/main.js` — keyboard/mouse input, fixed-step loop, drawing, sound triggers
- `src/assets.js` — loads the art and audio listed in `docs/assets.md` from `assets/` (supplied by the artist); missing assets fall back to drawn shapes / silence
- `tests/play_match.py` — headless Chromium (Playwright) run that plays full matches through the keyboard and checks every requirement; screenshots go to `tests/out/`

Run the check: `python3 tests/play_match.py --file` (needs `pip install playwright` and `playwright install chromium`).
